 BEAM-304A for the common R408W mutation in PKU, then https://t.co/Lxg3ci7Bvm", "url": "https://x.com/zhaoweiasu/status/2115467487764677012"}, {"author_id": "1709420611007545344", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:13:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115461545991782775", "2115462012838748634"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/RQHyacVtUC", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BrotherCliffS/status/2115462012838748634/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115462004903165952", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/RQHyacVtUC"}]}, "id": "2115462012838748634", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 71, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What CRISPR is\n\nCRISPR (Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats) is a gene-editing technology adapted from a natural bacterial immune system. \n\nIn bacteria, it stores fragments of viral DNA and uses them with CRISPR-associated (Cas) proteins (most famously Cas9) https://t.co/RQHyacVtUC", "url": "https://x.com/BrotherCliffS/status/2115462012838748634"}, {"author_id": "1709420611007545344", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:11:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115461545991782775", "2115462012838748634"], "id": "2115461545991782775", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What CRISPR is\n\nCRISPR (Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats) is a gene-editing technology adapted from a natural bacterial immune system. \n\nIn bacteria, it stores fragments of viral DNA and uses them with CRISPR-associated (Cas) proteins (most famously Cas9)", "url": "https://x.com/BrotherCliffS/status/2115461545991782775"}, {"author_id": "1464430347333083145", "created_at": "2026-10-27T02:49:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114912405411295521"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/RkBV7Ls8Cq", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Fintech03/status/2114912405411295521/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114910278181900288", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/RkBV7Ls8Cq"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/RkBV7Ls8Cq", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Fintech03/status/2114912405411295521/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114910438425305088", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/RkBV7Ls8Cq"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/RkBV7Ls8Cq", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Fintech03/status/2114912405411295521/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114910470377447424", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/RkBV7Ls8Cq"}]}, "id": "2114912405411295521", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 22, "impression_count": 4286, "like_count": 164, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 52}, "text": "A team in Cuttack has shown that an AI-designed enzyme can edit rice DNA in several different ways. They also regenerated edited plants and grew them to maturity.\n\nThe original enzyme came from Profluent Bio, an American company. The Indian work was adapting it for rice and https://t.co/RkBV7Ls8Cq", "url": "https://x.com/Fintech03/status/2114912405411295521"}, {"author_id": "1523638440503300096", "created_at": "2026-10-27T01:55:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114898626866507969"], "id": "2114898626866507969", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 84, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Prime Medicine has dosed the first patient with an in-body prime-editing therapy for Wilson disease — a one-time infusion that carries the editor to liver cells to fix the ATP7B mutation behind copper buildup. Nature calls it the first known use of prime editing directly inside a", "url": "https://x.com/Deep___White/status/2114898626866507969"}, {"author_id": "1597654998971604992", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:23:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115539867488952423"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "regulations.gov/document/FDA-2…", "end": 138, "ex